/** @defgroup bflat_ts_alignment bflat build - Alignment of memory accesses
 * @ingroup bflat_ts
 * @{
 *
 * @brief Tests that a load or a store wider than a byte is made at an address aligned for it.
 *
 *        The zkVMs that take the riscv32 build stop the guest on a misaligned
 *        access, so the compiler has to split one it cannot prove aligned:
 *        accesses marked as unaligned, packed structs, structs aligned to
 *        one or two bytes, addresses of unknown alignment. An emulator that
 *        allows misaligned accesses checks only the values.
 *
 *        A program prints "ALL PASS" and returns zero, or prints every
 *        failed check and returns non-zero. Where the compiler has a switch
 *        for what a program tests, a second run builds the same program with
 *        the switch the other way.
 *
 * @}
 */
